+\subsection{A task-independent audit layer}
+The principal training, checkpoint and web workflows target discrete-action LunarLander-v3. A separate \texttt{lunarlab.audit} layer accepts task adapters that define outcomes, metrics, diagnostics and reward-term factories. Through it, the reward accounting, seed and finite-value contracts, provenance record, fixed-seed policy audit, checkpoint selection, freezing (the same function the main pipeline uses), digest-checked final test, artifact export and verified replay apply to any Gymnasium task; a prespecified study protocol fixes the designs, learner, seeds and selection rule before training. A command (\texttt{lunarlab audit-artifact verify|reproduce}) checks an exported artifact before any episode runs. Learner seeds and environment seeds are recorded separately: SB3 re-seeds the environments when a model is built, so the layer sets the training environments' first-reset seeds afterwards and verifies them, while later training episodes continue each environment's random stream. Extending the complete application would additionally require generalizing run configuration, environment construction, episode schemas and the interface components.
 
