 \section{Research use and limitations}
-The hover experiment illustrates the intended research use. A researcher first identifies the incentive paid by the reward term, then verifies which validation-selected checkpoint was evaluated, and finally examines its reward components, strict landing outcomes and timeouts. Re-scoring a trajectory supports inspection of that incentive; artifact verification and re-evaluation test the identity and repeatability of the recorded evidence. These operations make the explanation of a failure inspectable from reward specification through observed behavior.
