 \section{Conclusion}
-LunarLab links reward specifications to component records, checkpoint selection to protected policy artifacts, and those artifacts to task outcomes. The LunarLander study illustrates how these links support investigation of a reward-design failure, while re-evaluation separates file integrity from numerical agreement and behavioral conclusions. The open implementation and exported artifacts make the demonstrated failure and the experimental process available for inspection and reuse.
